---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What data alexemm.com collects, why, who processes it, and how to exercise your rights. Short version: a contact form, and nothing else."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-09')}
>

  <h2>The short version</h2>

  <p>
    This site does not track you. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and embeds
    nothing from anyone else. The only personal data I ever receive is what you type
    into the contact form, and I use it to reply to you and nothing else.
  </p>

  <p>
    The longer version is below, because the law requires the detail and because you
    are entitled to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>

  <p>
    I am. Alexandros Emmanouilidis, based in Cyprus. I run this site personally. I am
    the data controller for anything described here.
  </p>

  <p>
    You can reach me through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    I do not have a Data Protection Officer, and I am not required to have one.
  </p>

  <h2>What I collect</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>If you use the contact form</strong>, I receive the name you give, the
    email address you give, and the message you write. That is it. There are no hidden
    fields, and the one field you cannot see is a spam trap that legitimate visitors
    never fill in.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>If you just read the site</strong>, my host records standard server log
    data: your IP address, the page requested, the time, your browser's user agent
    string. This is ordinary web server logging. I do not have a dashboard for it and
    I do not look at it.
  </p>

  <p>
    I do not collect special category data. I do not build profiles. I make no
    automated decisions about anyone. Nothing on this site is aimed at children.
  </p>

  <h2>Why, and on what legal basis</h2>

  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">What</th>
          <th scope="col">Why</th>
          <th scope="col">Legal basis</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Contact form submissions</td>
          <td>To read your message and reply to it</td>
          <td>
            Legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. If you write to me, replying is
            the obvious expected outcome, and it costs you nothing.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Server logs</td>
          <td>Keeping the site running and defending it against abuse</td>
          <td>Legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f) GDPR</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    If your message is about work, a placement or a commission, the basis may instead
    be Article 6(1)(b), because we would be taking steps towards a contract at your
    request. Either way, the handling is the same.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

  <p>
    I use three services. None of them sells your data and none of them uses it for
    their own purposes.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Netlify</strong> hosts the site and processes contact form submissions.
    Netlify's infrastructure is primarily in the United States, so submitting the form
    transfers your data outside the European Economic Area. Netlify acts as my
    processor under a Data Processing Agreement and relies on the European
    Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses as the transfer safeguard.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Microsoft</strong> provides the mailbox that form notifications and direct
    emails arrive in.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Porkbun</strong> is the domain registrar and runs the DNS. They do not
    receive your form data.
  </p>

  <p>
    Beyond those three, nobody. No advertising networks, no data brokers, no analytics
    companies, no CDNs serving fonts or scripts.
  </p>

  <p>
    I will disclose data to a public authority if a valid legal obligation requires
    it. That has never happened.
  </p>

  <h2>How long I keep it</h2>

  <p>
    Contact form submissions: 6 months from the date you send them, then deleted from
    Netlify and from my mailbox. If a message turns into an ongoing conversation or a
    working relationship, I keep it for as long as that relationship needs and then
    delete it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Server logs: retained by Netlify under their own retention schedule. I have no
    separate copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>

  <p>Under the GDPR you can ask me to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>give you a copy</strong> of the personal data I hold about you</li>
    <li><strong>correct</strong> anything inaccurate</li>
    <li><strong>delete</strong> it</li>
    <li><strong>restrict</strong> what I do with it</li>
    <li><strong>hand it over</strong> in a portable format</li>
    <li>
      <strong>stop</strong> processing it, where I am relying on legitimate interests
      - which is most of what is above
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and say which one you want. I will
    respond within one month, as required. There is no charge, and I will not ask you
    to justify the request.
  </p>

  <p>
    Given the scale of this operation, "delete it" in practice means I find your
    message in two places and remove it from both. It is not a bureaucratic process.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you think I have handled your data badly, you can complain to the Cypriot
    supervisory authority:
  </p>

  <div class="legal-address">
    <p><strong>Office of the Commissioner for Personal Data Protection</strong></p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.dataprotection.gov.cy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        dataprotection.gov.cy
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>I would rather you told me first, but that is your call, not mine.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>

  <p>There are none. See the <a href="/cookies">cookie statement</a>.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>

  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS with HSTS enabled. It is a static site, so there is
    no database and no application server to compromise. Form submissions are held in
    Netlify's dashboard behind my account, which is protected by a strong unique
    password and two-factor authentication.
  </p>

  <p>
    I cannot promise perfect security, because nobody honestly can. I can promise
    there is very little here to steal.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    If I change this policy I will update the date at the top. If a change is
    significant, I will say what changed rather than quietly swapping the text.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
